Verse 1:
[G]To God [D7]be the [G]glory, great [D]things He hath [G]done!
[G]So [C]loved He the [G]world that He [Am]gave us His [D]Son,
[D7]Who yielded His life [G]an atonement [D]for [G]sin,
[G]And opened [C]the lifegate [G/D]that all may [D7]go [G]in.

Refrain:
[G]Praise the Lord, praise the Lord,
[Am]let the [G]earth hear [D]his voice!
[D]Praise the [D7]Lord, praise the Lord,
[Bm]let the [D7/A]people [G]rejoice!
[G]O come [D7]to the [G]Father thru [D]Jesus the [G]Son,
[G]and [C]give him the [G/D]glory, great things he [D7]hath [G]done!

Verse 2:
[G]O perfect [D7]redemption, [G/B]the [D]purchase of [G]blood,
[G]to every [C]believer [G]the [Am]promise of [D]God;
[D7]the vilest offender [G]who truly [D]believes,
[G]that moment [C]from Jesus [D]a [G/D]pardon receives.

Verse 3:
[G]Great things [D7]he hath [G]taught us, great [D]things he hath [G]done,
[G]and [C]great our rejoicing [G]thru [Am]Jesus the [D]Son;
[D7]but [G]purer, [D7]and [G]higher, and [D]greater will [G]be
[G]our [C]wonder, our [G/D]transport, when Jesus [D7]we [G]see.
